{{Lua|Module:ForAllUtaite}}
A metatemplate in the style of {{t|Main other}}: it outputs its first parameter on pages that transclude {{t|Utaite}}, and its second parameter on all other pages. Useful inside maintenance/marker templates to apply different categories (or text) to utaite pages versus everything else.
== Syntax ==
{{T|ForAllUtaite|v1=|v2=}}

== Examples ==
<pre>{{ForAllUtaite|[[Category:Utaite with outdated covered song list]]|[[Category:Youtaite with outdated covered song list]]}}</pre>
On a page using {{t|Utaite}} this adds [[:Category:Utaite with outdated covered song list]]; on any other page it adds [[:Category:Youtaite with outdated covered song list]].

=== Demo mode ===
Use <code>demo=</code> to force a branch (for documentation and testing):
* {{T|ForAllUtaite|v1=utaite text|v2=other text|demo=utaite}} → {{ForAllUtaite|utaite text|other text|demo=utaite}}
* {{T|ForAllUtaite|v1=utaite text|v2=other text|demo=other}} → {{ForAllUtaite|utaite text|other text|demo=other}}

== Notes ==
* The check reads the current page's own wikitext, so it reacts immediately when {{t|Utaite}} is added or removed.
* In the Template, Module and MediaWiki namespaces the template outputs nothing (unless <code>demo=</code> is set), so templates embedding it do not categorize their own pages.

=== Dependencies ===
* [[Module:ForAllUtaite]]

